I think the essential problem is that rather few weapons are generated
randomly, the vast majority start out in monster inventories, and, IIRC,
no monster is likely to be generated with a silver dagger(I *think* I've
seen a critter drop a silver dagger once or twice, in ~20 ascensions, but
I'm not sure).  Also, IIRC, silver daggers are 0.3% of randomly generated 
weapons, so you'd need about 300 truly randomly generated weapons to get one 
silver dagger.  There usually aren't that many randomly generated....unless 
you polypile.  Generating a thousand random weapons* can be pretty easy if Ludios
exists in your game.

*Not all at once.

If you really really want a bunch of silver daggers, you can. 

(a) polypile the hell out of Ludios and the castle.  I usually do this, although
not for the purpose of finding silver daggers, but I usually see 4 or so
if I poly the pile a 'til it fits on 1 page.  Poly the mines weapons, too, if
you're desperate.  #name and unstack the stacked weapons in the pile, first.

(b) Wish for them.  You can wish for multiples.

If having a stack of silver throwing daggers is something you'd like to do,
I wouldn't imagine it would be impossible to collect 10 or 12 or so.

Silver is so powerful that I'm sure it's *meant* to be a lot of work
to be able to throw silver daggers on a regular basis.


